// REJECTS: Unexpected token
//
// A Database body is `(include | includeStore)* (schema | table | view | join | ...)*`.
// The includes are not a set of statements that may appear anywhere -- they are a PREFIX.
// This puts one after a Table.
//
// Nothing about the surface suggests order matters: both are top-level entries in the same
// parenthesised body, and every other list in this grammar is unordered. A rewrite that
// loops "read the next Database entry, dispatch on its keyword" accepts this without ever
// noticing it made a choice. The legal form (include first) parses.
###Relational
Database fixture::neg::IncludeLate
(
   Table T (ID VARCHAR(32) PRIMARY KEY)
   include fixture::neg::Other
)
